# Every secret and parameter the deployment needs — NAMES ONLY.
#
# There is no value anywhere in this file and none may ever be added to it. It
# is the checklist you work through at approval time, and the inventory you
# work through at teardown.
#
# The distinction that matters:
#
#   SECRET      lives in AWS Secrets Manager, is referenced from a task
#               definition's `secrets` block by ARN, and is read by the ECS
#               *execution* role before the container starts. It never appears
#               in the image, in `environment`, in a log line, or in this repo.
#   PARAMETER   is non-sensitive configuration. It goes in the task
#               definition's `environment` block in plain sight, because hiding
#               a region or a model ID buys nothing and costs clarity.
#   DERIVED     the application never receives it at all. It comes from the
#               task role through the container credentials endpoint.
#
# `../.env.example` is the same list for local development. This file is the
# deployed shape of it.


# ===========================================================================
# SECRET — AWS Secrets Manager
# ===========================================================================

# The CockroachDB connection URL. One secret, one value, plaintext string (not
# JSON) so the task definition can reference it without a JSON key.
#
#   suggested secret name:  swarm-brain/database-url
#   referenced as:          <DATABASE_URL_SECRET_ARN> in both
#                           ecs-task-definition.api.json and
#                           ecs-task-definition.worker.json
#   injected as:            SWARMBRAIN_DATABASE_URL
#
# The URL must carry `sslmode=verify-full`. A URL with `require`, `prefer`, or
# no sslmode at all authenticates the client to the server but not the server
# to the client, and is not acceptable for a deployment that claims accountable
# memory. CockroachDB Cloud Basic uses a publicly trusted CA, so `verify-full`
# works against the container's system trust store with no CA file.
#
# The SQL user in the URL must be scoped to the demo database. Do not put a
# cluster admin in here. See ../README.md.
SWARMBRAIN_DATABASE_URL

# The HMAC secret that signs and verifies agent run tokens. Every token the
# console, the MCP bridge and the smoke script present is minted from this
# value, so it is the single credential that gates every /v1 route.
#
#   suggested secret name:  swarm-brain/token-secret
#   referenced as:          <TOKEN_SECRET_ARN>
#   injected as:            SWARMBRAIN_TOKEN_SECRET
#
# At least 16 random bytes. Generate it, never type it:
#   python3 -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))'
#
# The API and the worker MUST share the same value. They are separate services
# reading the same secret ARN, which is what keeps them in step.
#
# This is NOT the local development secret. `local-demo-secret-0123456789`
# appears in this repository's documentation as a local placeholder and must
# never reach a deployed task.
SWARMBRAIN_TOKEN_SECRET


# ===========================================================================
# PARAMETER — task definition `environment`, non-sensitive
# ===========================================================================

# Backend selection. Fail-closed and mandatory: the process refuses to start
# without it rather than defaulting to the in-memory backend, which would look
# healthy and store nothing. Always "cockroach" in a deployment.
SWARMBRAIN_BACKEND

# Bind address and port for the API. The image already sets 0.0.0.0:8080 and
# the task definition restates it, because a silent 127.0.0.1 under awsvpc is
# unreachable from the load balancer and produces a target-health failure that
# reads like an application problem.
SWARMBRAIN_HOST
SWARMBRAIN_PORT

# Dense-recall provider. "bedrock" activates
# src/swarmbrain/adapters/embeddings/bedrock.py, which reaches Bedrock with the
# task role's credentials. "none" and "deterministic" are the other legal
# values; "deterministic" is a local fixture, never a deployment.
SWARMBRAIN_EMBEDDINGS

# Bedrock embedding model. `amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` — the ID in the
# committed adapter, not a free choice: the dense projection stamps every
# stored vector with the model that produced it, so changing this invalidates
# existing vectors. It must also match the model ARN in
# iam/task-role-policy.json.
SWARMBRAIN_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL

# Embedding width. CockroachDB requires exactly 1024 here — config rejects any
# other value when the backend is cockroach and embeddings are enabled, because
# it must match the VECTOR(1024) column and its ANN index. Changing it after
# vectors exist is a reindex, not a config change.
SWARMBRAIN_EMBEDDINGS_DIMENSIONS

# Region passed to the boto3 bedrock-runtime client. Set it to the deployment
# region; an unset value makes boto3 guess from its own resolution chain, which
# is one more thing that can silently differ between local and deployed.
SWARMBRAIN_AWS_REGION

# The hosted-demo switch. `enabled` turns on the console's demo trigger so a
# judge can drive the scripted swarm from the page without a shell. Leave it
# unset (or anything other than `enabled`) for a plain read-only console.
#
# Verified against src/swarmbrain/config.py: the trigger is on only when the
# value case-folds to exactly "enabled". Any other value — including "true",
# "1" and "yes" — leaves it off. That is deliberate and fail-closed, and it is
# the opposite of how the other boolean settings parse.
SWARMBRAIN_CONSOLE_DEMO

# Connection pool bounds, per process. The API and the worker are separate
# tasks with separate pools; CockroachDB Cloud Basic has a connection limit, so
# these two plus your own psql sessions must stay under it.
SWARMBRAIN_DATABASE_POOL_MIN_SIZE
SWARMBRAIN_DATABASE_POOL_MAX_SIZE

# Operator-owned ingestion policy. These are never accepted from an HTTP or MCP
# request body — that is the point of them living here.
SWARMBRAIN_INGEST_TRUST
SWARMBRAIN_INGEST_USE_PROVIDER
SWARMBRAIN_INGEST_CHUNK_CHARS
SWARMBRAIN_INGEST_PRIORITY

# Dense retrieval tuning. Change either only against the exact oracle and
# judged runs — see ../../docs/retrieval-evaluation.md.
SWARMBRAIN_RETRIEVAL_DENSE_MIN_SIMILARITY
SWARMBRAIN_RETRIEVAL_DENSE_ANN_BEAM_SIZE

# Worker-only. SWARMBRAIN_WORKER_ID is deliberately NOT set in the task
# definition: unset, each process generates its own `worker-<uuid4>` at start,
# which is exactly what you want when ECS replaces a task. Pinning it would
# make two overlapping tasks during a rolling deploy claim the same worker
# identity. SWARMBRAIN_WORKER_LIMIT must remain 1 until extraction leases
# heartbeat.
SWARMBRAIN_WORKER_ID
SWARMBRAIN_WORKER_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS
SWARMBRAIN_WORKER_LEASE_SECONDS
SWARMBRAIN_WORKER_RETRY_DELAY_SECONDS
SWARMBRAIN_WORKER_LIMIT


# ===========================================================================
# DERIVED — never configured, never stored
# ===========================================================================

# AWS credentials for Bedrock come from the ECS task role, which boto3
# discovers through AWS_CONTAINER_CREDENTIALS_RELATIVE_URI. ECS sets that
# variable itself.
#
# There is no AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, no AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY and no
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN in this deployment — not in the image, not in a task
# definition, not in a secret. If one appears, something has gone wrong.
#
# The AWS_* keys in ../.env.example are for an operator's laptop running
# scripts/bedrock_smoke.py before this deployment exists. They are not part of
# the deployed shape.


# ===========================================================================
# Non-AWS accounts referenced by the deployment
# ===========================================================================

# CockroachDB Cloud: the Basic cluster, its SQL user, and the read-only Managed
# MCP connection. Managed outside AWS, in the CockroachDB Cloud console or
# through `ccloud` — see ../../scripts/provision_cloud.sh. Billed separately
# from the AWS account.
#
# ECR: the image repository. No credential is stored; `aws ecr
# get-login-password` mints a short-lived token from the operator's own
# identity at push time.
